7
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:57,000
The Biggest Little Farm is a 2018 American
documentary film, directed by John Chester.

8
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:30,000
The film profiles the life of John Chester and his wife Molly as they acquire and
establish themselves on Apricot Lane Farms in Moorpark, California.

9
00:40:57,000 --> 00:41:03,000
The film premiered on September 1, 2018, at the Telluride Film Festival.

10
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
It had its second screening at the 2018 Toronto International Film Festival, where it
was named second runner-up for the People's Choice Award: Documentaries.

11
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:09,000
It was selected as the Opening Night film at Doc NYC in November 2018.

12
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
The film was screened as part of the Spotlight Section
at the 2019 Sundance Film Festival.

13
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:15,000
It also screened at the 29th New Orleans Film Festival on October 24, 2018.

14
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:48,000
The film was acquired for theatrical distribution by the independent film company
Neon, and was released on May 10, 2019 in Los Angeles and New York.

15
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
The film expanded into Austin, Boston, Chicago, Dallas, Denver, Houston, Minneapolis, Nashville, Philadelphia, Phoenix,
Portland, San Diego, San Francisco and Washington, D.C., on May 17 and additional markets throughout May and June.

16
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
The film was acquired by The Exchange for international distribution.

17
01:17:21,000 --> 01:17:27,000
A sequel special, The Biggest Little Farm: The
Return, was released in 2022 on Disney+.

18
01:21:54,000 --> 01:22:00,000
The film explores themes of farm, california, social
documentary, farming, sustainability.

19
01:26:27,000 --> 01:26:33,000
The tone is uplifting.
